  "convention": "Arithmetic square roots over the reals; moving a negative coefficient inside requires keeping its minus sign outside.",
  "solutions": [
    {
      "exercise": "971",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "answer": "\\sqrt{15}", "derivation": "60=4*15, so 0.5*2sqrt(15)=sqrt(15)."},
        {"label": "b", "answer": "10\\sqrt6", "derivation": "150=25*6, so 2*5sqrt(6)=10sqrt(6)."},
        {"label": "c", "answer": "0.1\\sqrt3", "derivation": "300=100*3, so 0.01*10sqrt(3)=0.1sqrt(3)."},
        {"label": "d", "answer": "\\sqrt{15}", "derivation": "375=25*15, so 0.2*5sqrt(15)=sqrt(15)."},
        {"label": "e", "answer": "\\frac{3\\sqrt3}{4}", "derivation": "The mixed number is 27/16=9*3/16; the positive square root is 3sqrt(3)/4."},
        {"label": "f", "answer": "\\frac{7\\sqrt2}{9}", "derivation": "The mixed number is 98/81=49*2/81; the root is 7sqrt(2)/9."},
        {"label": "g", "answer": "\\frac{5\\sqrt3}{6}", "derivation": "The mixed number is 25/12=25*3/36; the root is 5sqrt(3)/6."},
        {"label": "h", "answer": "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}8", "derivation": "The mixed number is 45/32=9*10/64; the root is 3sqrt(10)/8."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "972",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "answer": "\\frac15\\sqrt{200}<10\\sqrt8", "derivation": "The two positive quantities reduce to 2sqrt(2) and 20sqrt(2)."},
        {"label": "b", "answer": "7\\sqrt{\\frac{32}{49}}=0.8\\sqrt{50}", "derivation": "Both quantities reduce to 4sqrt(2)."},
        {"label": "c", "answer": "0.5\\sqrt{108}<9\\sqrt3", "derivation": "The first quantity is 3sqrt(3), less than 9sqrt(3)."},
        {"label": "d", "answer": "\\frac52\\sqrt{63}<4.5\\sqrt{28}", "derivation": "The quantities reduce to (15/2)sqrt(7) and 9sqrt(7); 15/2<9."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "973",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "answer": "\\sqrt{50}", "derivation": "The positive factor 5/2 enters as its square: (25/4)*8=50."},
        {"label": "b", "answer": "\\sqrt8", "derivation": "The positive factor 2/3 enters as its square: (4/9)*18=8."},
        {"label": "c", "answer": "-\\sqrt{3x^4}", "domain": "x real", "derivation": "x^2 is nonnegative; move x^2 inside as x^4, retaining the leading minus, including x=0."},
        {"label": "d", "answer": "\\sqrt{a^3}", "domain": "a>0", "derivation": "1/a must be defined and nonnegative, hence a>0. Moving a^2 inside gives a^4/a=a^3."},
        {"label": "e", "answer": "-\\sqrt{3a^3}", "domain": "a>=0", "derivation": "The radical requires a>=0; -3a is nonpositive. Keep its minus and move 3a inside: 9a^2*(a/3)=3a^3."},
        {"label": "f", "answer": "-\\sqrt{-3a^3}", "domain": "a<=0", "derivation": "The radical requires a<=0, so 3a is nonpositive. Move -3a inside and retain a minus: 9a^2*(-a/3)=-3a^3."},
        {"label": "g", "answer": "\\sqrt{ab^3}", "domain": "a>0,b>0", "derivation": "ab>0, so its square enters: a^2*b^2*(b/a)=a*b^3."},
        {"label": "h", "answer": "\\sqrt{2a^3b}", "domain": "a<0,b<0", "derivation": "2ab>0 and a/(2b)>0. Squaring the outer factor gives 4a^2*b^2*a/(2b)=2a^3*b>0."},
        {"label": "i", "answer": "undefined over the reals under the stated conditions", "domain": "a<0,b<0", "derivation": "Both 1/a and 1/b are negative, so their sum is strictly negative. The original real square root does not exist; do not invent a changed sign or domain.", "source_anomaly": true}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "974",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "answer": "\\sqrt{30}<\\frac23\\sqrt{72}<7\\sqrt2", "derivation": "The positive quantities have squares 30,32,98 in increasing order."},
        {"label": "b", "answer": "\\frac12\\sqrt{62}<\\sqrt{17}<5\\sqrt{\\frac72}", "derivation": "Their positive squares are 31/2,17,175/2, with 31/2<17<175/2."},
        {"label": "c", "answer": "8\\sqrt{0.2}<\\frac25\\sqrt{250}<\\sqrt{41}", "derivation": "The positive squares are 64/5,40,41, with 64/5<40<41."},
        {"label": "d", "answer": "12\\sqrt{0.5}<\\sqrt{89}<\\frac34\\sqrt{160}", "derivation": "The positive squares are 72,89,90."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "975",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "answer": "b=0 with any real a, or b>0 and a>=0", "derivation": "The right radical requires b>=0. At b=0 both sides are zero for every a. At b>0, sqrt(a^2*b)=|a|sqrt(b)=a sqrt(b) exactly when a>=0."},
        {"label": "b", "answer": "b=0 with any real a, or b>0 and a<=0", "derivation": "Both sides require b>=0. At b=0 both vanish; at b>0 the equality |a|=-a holds exactly when a<=0."},
        {"label": "c", "answer": "b>=0 with any real a", "derivation": "b>=0 is necessary for the right radical, even if a=0. Then sqrt(a^4*b)=|a^2|sqrt(b)=a^2sqrt(b) for every a."},
        {"label": "d", "answer": "b=0 with any real a, or b>0 and a>=0", "derivation": "b>=0 is required. At b=0 both vanish. Otherwise sqrt(a^6*b)=|a^3|sqrt(b)=a^3sqrt(b) exactly when a>=0."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "976",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "answer": "-3a\\sqrt b", "domain": "a<0,b>0", "derivation": "sqrt(9a^2*b)=3|a|sqrt(b)=-3a sqrt(b)."},
        {"label": "b", "answer": "5ab\\sqrt b", "domain": "a>0,b>0", "derivation": "25a^2*b^3=(5ab)^2*b and 5ab>0."},
        {"label": "c", "answer": "12ab\\sqrt{ab}", "domain": "a<0,b<0", "derivation": "ab>0 and 144a^3*b^3=(12ab)^2*(ab), so the extracted factor is 12ab."},
        {"label": "d", "answer": "4a^2b\\sqrt{2b}", "domain": "a<0,b>0", "derivation": "32a^4*b^3=(4a^2*b)^2*(2b); 4a^2*b is positive under the source conditions."},
        {"label": "e", "answer": "undefined over the reals under the stated condition", "domain": "c<0", "derivation": "c^2>0, so -8c^2<0. The original radical is not real; retain the printed minus and domain.", "source_anomaly": true},
        {"label": "f", "answer": "-m^3\\sqrt{-5m}", "domain": "m<0", "derivation": "-5m^7=m^6*(-5m), with -5m>0. The extracted |m^3| equals -m^3."},
        {"label": "g", "answer": "(x-1)\\sqrt2", "domain": "x>=1", "derivation": "sqrt(2(x-1)^2)=|x-1|sqrt(2) and x-1>=0."},
        {"label": "h", "answer": "(1-y)\\sqrt7", "domain": "y<1", "derivation": "sqrt(7(y-1)^2)=|y-1|sqrt(7) and y-1<0."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "977",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "answer": "\\sqrt{2(x-1)}", "domain": "x>1", "derivation": "The source outer factor x-1 is positive. Its square enters and cancels the nonzero denominator."},
        {"label": "b", "answer": "\\sqrt{4(x+5)}", "domain": "x>-5", "derivation": "x+5>0; move its square inside: (x+5)^2*4/(x+5)=4(x+5)."},
        {"label": "c", "answer": "-\\sqrt{x(x+2)}", "domain": "x<-2", "derivation": "The original outer factor x+2 is negative although the task says to move a positive factor. Write it as -(-x-2), move the positive -x-2 inside, and retain the minus. The inner result (x+2)^2*x/(x+2)=x(x+2)>0.", "source_wording_watch": "Do not drop the minus or silently change x<-2."},
        {"label": "d", "answer": "\\sqrt{5x(x-4)}", "domain": "x>4", "derivation": "x-4>0; entering its square gives (x-4)^2*5x/(x-4)=5x(x-4)."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "978",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "answer": "sqrt(3(b-1)^2) for b>=1; -sqrt(3(b-1)^2) for b<1", "domain": "b real", "derivation": "The coefficient b-1 changes sign at 1. Move its magnitude inside and retain the sign; equality holds at b=1 as zero."},
        {"label": "b", "answer": "sqrt(5(a+2)^2) for a>=-2; -sqrt(5(a+2)^2) for a<-2", "domain": "a real", "derivation": "The coefficient a+2 changes sign at -2; squaring alone would lose the negative branch."},
        {"label": "c", "answer": "\\sqrt{x(x+1)^2}", "domain": "x>=0", "derivation": "The original radical requires x>=0, which makes x+1>0. Its square enters without a minus."},
        {"label": "d", "answer": "-\\sqrt{-x(x-2)^2}", "domain": "x<=0", "derivation": "The original radical requires x<=0, so x-2<0. Move 2-x inside and retain the minus, including x=0."},
        {"label": "e", "answer": "-\\sqrt{\\frac{3a(1-a)}{1+a}}", "domain": "0<a<1", "derivation": "a-1<0 and 1-a^2>0. Keep the minus while entering (1-a)^2: 3a(1-a)^2/((1-a)(1+a))=3a(1-a)/(1+a)."},
        {"label": "f", "answer": "\\sqrt{\\frac{5a(a-2)}{a+2}}", "domain": "-2<a<0", "derivation": "2-a>0. Enter its square into the positive original radical. Using a^2-4=(a-2)(a+2) gives 5a(2-a)^2/(a^2-4)=5a(a-2)/(a+2)>0. Both canceled factors are nonzero in the stated domain."}
      ]
    }
  ],
